course: dictionary
lesson: 687
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear two coats. Bamboo can mean a plant, or the material made from that plant. Read the words around it to find out which. «The giant panda sat chewing bamboo in the forest.» Chewing and forest are your clues, so bamboo means the plant.
explain: «The shelf was built from strong, light bamboo and fixed with screws.» Built from and fixed tell you that bamboo is something you make things out of. Ask yourself: is this thing growing, or is it made? The sentence clues answer that.
explain: Context can also show you what a word is like. «Bamboo bends in the wind but does not break.» Bends and does not break tell you bamboo is strong and flexible. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are right.
fact: Bamboo is a very tall, fast-growing plant, a kind of giant grass with hard, hollow stems.
fact: Bamboo is also the strong, light material made from those stems, used for building, furniture and fishing rods.
fact: «Real giant pandas eat almost only bamboo, about 12 to 38 kilograms a day.»
fact: Some kinds of bamboo grow almost a metre in a single day, which makes it one of the fastest-growing plants on Earth.
fact: In Asian stories and art, bamboo is a sign of strength, because it bends in the wind but does not break.
exercise: «Protecting and joining up bamboo forests in China helped giant pandas.» In this sentence, what is bamboo? | *A tall plant that grows in forests | A strong, light material for building | A kind of bear | A sweet fruit from the jungle
exercise: «The chair was made of bamboo, so it was light to carry.» What is bamboo here? | A bird that sings in the trees | A drum played at festivals | A wild animal from China | *A strong, light material made from plant stems
exercise: «Giant pandas eat almost only bamboo, so they must eat a huge amount.» Why must a panda eat so much bamboo? | Because pandas do not like to eat | Because bamboo is made of metal | *Because bamboo gives it little goodness, so it needs a lot | Because bamboo is very rare
test: «The panda sat in the bamboo forest, munching happily.» In this sentence, bamboo means | A strong material for furniture | *A tall plant with hard, hollow stems | A metal tool | A toothbrush
test: «The toothbrush handle was made of bamboo.» Which meaning fits best? | A type of drum | *The material made from bamboo stems | A giant panda | The plant that grows in the forest
exam: «Bamboo bends in the wind but does not break, so in old stories it is a sign of strength.» Which description fits bamboo best? | Weak and easily broken | Only found in cold places | Heavy and slow to grow | *Strong and flexible, bending without breaking
